<!--
  Not_Returned added 31 July, session 10, ratified.

  A row the model never reported is not an abstained row. It was carrying Outcome =
  Abstained with Abstention_Reason = not_returned, and the field description explained that
  counting abstentions by outcome would overcount. That is documenting a trap rather than
  removing one: the plausible query was the wrong query, and the schema was the thing making
  it wrong. Now the plausible reading is the true one.

  Abstained still means a judgment about evidence: the reader looked and either found
  nothing bearing on the proposition or could not resolve what it found. Not_Returned means
  the reader never answered, which is a fact about the charter.

  Nothing was backfilled, and nothing needed to be: not_returned had never been written to a
  live row when this landed.
-->
